constructors.comment:
Constructor creating theSize elements initialized to theValue. Equivalent to std::vector(n, val).
@param theSize number of elements to construct
@param theValue value to initialize each element with

instanceMethods.comment:
Change the number of elements, filling new slots with theValue. If theSize > `Size()`, new elements are copy-constructed from theValue. If theSize < `Size()`, excess elements are destroyed.
@param theSize new number of elements
@param theValue value to fill new elements with

Append a copy of theValue to the end.
@param theValue element to append
@returns reference to the appended element

Set value at theIndex. If theIndex >= `Size()`, the vector is extended.
@param theIndex element index (0-based)
@param theValue value to set
@returns reference to the element

Insert theValue before theIndex, shifting elements right.
@param theIndex insertion position (0-based)
@param theValue element to insert

Insert theValue after theIndex, shifting elements right.
@param theIndex position after which to insert (0-based)
@param theValue element to insert

Remove elements in range [theFrom, theTo), shifting subsequent elements left.
@param theFrom start index (inclusive, 0-based)
@param theTo end index (exclusive, 0-based)

